Upstream builds std from source on release (-Zbuild-std), which needs a
nightly rustc with the rust-src component. MacPorts ships stable rust
without rust-src, so keep the prebuilt std; RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 (set in the
Portfile) unlocks the nightly-only -Z flags and #![feature] gates that the
rest of the build uses. Homebrew-core instead requires rustup and builds
with upstream's pinned nightly.

The workspace denies all warnings as errors. Stable rustc (1.97) predates
some lints known to upstream's pinned nightly (e.g.
suspicious_runtime_symbol_definitions), and -D warnings turns those
unknown-lints diagnostics into hard errors, so downgrade to warn.
--- scripts/build/rust.ts.orig
+++ scripts/build/rust.ts
@@ -414,7 +414,10 @@
     profile.name,
     "--locked",
   ];
+  // MacPorts: stable rustc cannot -Zbuild-std (needs nightly + rust-src).
+  // Homebrew-core instead requires rustup and builds with upstream's pinned
+  // nightly.
-  if (tier3 || cfg.release || cfg.asan) {
+  if (false) {
     // Rebuild std from source (cargoBuildStdArg) because:
     // tier3:   no prebuilt `rust-std` exists.
     // release: prebuilt std is native code built for generic x86-64 with no
--- Cargo.toml.orig
+++ Cargo.toml
@@ -200,7 +200,8 @@
 # Every rustc warning is an error. Individual lints below can override this
 # back to "warn" (their priority 0 beats the group's -1) where a warning level
 # is intentional.
+# MacPorts: unknown-lints on stable rustc must not be hard errors.
-warnings = { level = "deny", priority = -1 }
+warnings = { level = "warn", priority = -1 }
 # `bun_asan` / `bun_debug` / `socket_fault_injection` are set via RUSTFLAGS
 # (`--cfg=...` + `--check-cfg=cfg(...)`) by scripts/build/rust.ts; register
 # them here so a plain `cargo build` / `cargo check` (without those flags)
